	(text_box "The whole sensing chain lives on this sheet: shunt -> OPA -> ADC, plus BEMF, POT and NTC.\n\n- The shunt is the ONLY tie between PGND and GND, so all motor return current has to cross it. Don't add another tie in layout. The full layout rules (PGND island, cap returns, Kelvin routing) live in the DRV sheet notes.\n- Lots of DNPs on purpose. This is a swap-and-measure board, populated values are just the starting point.\n- R1/R2 are 0R walls in front of the amp. If they ever become real resistors, swap BOTH to the same value (thinfilm), or the arms go out of balance.\n- Cc 22pF is the fast config, about 3x faster than the validated rev-B damping. If it rings, stack the 47pF pads to get back on known-good ground.\n- VREF sits at ~500mV. Stack Rd3 to drop it to 250mV.\n- Precision money goes to the shunt + Rg/Rf quad only. Everything else is offset error and boot cal eats it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 29.21 0)
		(size 72.39 134.6199)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bfcdfb10-513c-4ea4-8592-ef41fde00e6f")
	)
